<!-- SECTION 2: OVERVIEW / INTRO + TL;DR -->
<section class="content-section" id="overview-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">GSTAT Appeal Filing in Ranchi - Overview</h2>
<div class="highlight-box" style="background:var(--orange-light);border-left:4px solid var(--orange);padding:20px 24px;border-radius:var(--radius-md);margin-bottom:24px;">
    <p style="font-weight:600;color:var(--blue);margin-bottom:8px;">TL;DR</p>
    <p>The Ranchi GSTAT Bench is the sole appellate tribunal for all GST disputes from 24 Jharkhand districts - India's mining and heavy industry heartland. From the steel mills of Jamshedpur and Bokaro to the coal mines of Dhanbad, Jharkhand generates significant GST enforcement activity. File Form APL-05 on efiling.gstat.gov.in within 3 months. Pre-deposit of 20% under S.112(8) is mandatory. Patron Accounting's CA team handles proceedings end-to-end with mining and steel sector expertise.</p>
</div>
<div class="table-responsive-wrapper"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>Bench</td><td>Ranchi GSTAT Bench (Jharkhand State Bench)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Jurisdiction</td><td>All 24 districts of Jharkhand</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Circuit Bench</td><td>None - Ranchi is the sole bench</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Bench Status</td><td>Operational. Technical Member (Centre): Bijoy Bihari Mohapatra. Members directed to join January 2026.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Pre-deposit</td><td>20% of disputed tax under S.112(8) CGST Act (cumulative). Cap: Rs 20 crore each CGST and SGST.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Limitation Period</td><td>3 months from date of order under S.112(1). Backlog appeals: deadline 30 June 2026.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Filing Mode</td><td>Online only via efiling.gstat.gov.in - Form APL-05</td></tr>
        <tr><td>SGST Authority</td><td>Commissioner of Commercial Taxes, Government of Jharkhand, Ranchi</td></tr>
        <tr><td>CGST Commissionerates</td><td>Ranchi Commissionerate (21 districts + Dhanbad Sub-Commissionerate) + Jamshedpur Commissionerate (3 districts)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>State Legislation</td><td>Jharkhand Goods and Services Tax Act, 2017 (JGST Act)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Jharkhand's economy is anchored by mining, steel, heavy engineering, and cement manufacturing. The CGST Ranchi Zone covers the state through two commissionerates - the Ranchi Commissionerate (with a Dhanbad Sub-Commissionerate) handles 21 districts, while the Jamshedpur Commissionerate covers 3 districts in the Singhbhum region. Mining royalty classification, ITC on mining inputs, inter-state mineral supply disputes, and steel sector classification issues are the most frequent demand categories. GSTAT President Justice (Retd.) Sanjaya Kumar Mishra was formerly Chief Justice of the Jharkhand High Court.</p>
            </div>
    </div>
</section>

