<!-- SECTION 4: WHO NEEDS THIS -->
<section class="content-section" id="who-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
                <h2 class="section-title" id="who-needs-section">Who Needs GSTAT Appeal Filing at the Ranchi Bench</h2><p>Any registered taxpayer or GST-registered business in Jharkhand that has received an unfavourable order from the First Appellate Authority under Section 107 or the Revisional Authority under Section 108 of the CGST/JGST Act can file a second appeal before the Ranchi GSTAT Bench under Section 112.</p><p>The Ranchi bench covers all 24 districts - from the state capital Ranchi, Jamshedpur (Tata Steel and Adityapur Industrial Area), Bokaro (SAIL Bokaro Steel Plant), Dhanbad (India's Coal Capital), and Hazaribagh to the tribal and mineral-rich districts of West Singhbhum (iron ore), Giridih and Koderma (mica capital), and the Santhal Parganas region. See also <a href="/gstat-appeal-filing/patna">GSTAT appeal filing in Patna</a> for the neighbouring Bihar bench and <a href="/gstat-appeal-filing/kolkata">GSTAT appeal filing in Kolkata</a>.</p><h3>Common Demand Categories in Jharkhand</h3><ul><li>Mining sector ITC disputes - classification of mining royalty payments under GST, ITC reversal on mining equipment and explosives</li><li>Steel industry classification disputes from Jamshedpur and Bokaro - HSN on semi-finished and finished steel products</li><li>Coal sector demands from Dhanbad - ITC on coal washing and transportation</li><li>Heavy engineering and cement sector disputes from the Adityapur-Gamharia industrial belt</li><li>E-way bill violations on mineral and coal transport across districts</li><li>Adverse orders on <a href="/gst-notice">GST notice</a> responses requiring tribunal appeal</li></ul>
            </div>
    </div>
</section>

