                <h2 class="section-title" id="services-section">GSTAT Appeal Filing Services at Ranchi Bench</h2><div class="table-responsive-wrapper"><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>What We Do</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Appealability Assessment</td><td>Review demand order from CGST Ranchi, Dhanbad Sub-Commissionerate, CGST Jamshedpur, or Jharkhand Commercial Taxes. Confirm grounds under S.112 with mining and steel sector expertise.</td></tr><tr><td>Pre-deposit Computation</td><td>Strategic computation of 20% under S.112(8). High-value mining and steel demands require careful planning. Hardship waiver guidance.</td></tr><tr><td>Form APL-05 Drafting</td><td>Draft grounds specific to mining royalty GST, steel HSN classification, coal ITC, and cement industry disputes. Use GSTAT offline Excel utility.</td></tr><tr><td>E-Filing Portal Navigation</td><td>End-to-end filing on <a href="https://efiling.gstat.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">efiling.gstat.gov.in</a>. All Jharkhand filings route to Ranchi (no circuit bench).</td></tr><tr><td>Bench Appearance (Ranchi)</td><td>Of-counsel GST litigation specialists attend admission, stay applications, and final arguments at the Ranchi bench.</td></tr><tr><td>Commissionerate Respondent ID</td><td>Correctly identify Ranchi Commissionerate, Dhanbad Sub-Commissionerate, or Jamshedpur Commissionerate as respondent.</td></tr><tr><td>Mining Sector Specialisation</td><td>Mining royalty GST classification grounds referencing the Supreme Court MADA ruling and CGST Act provisions.</td></tr><tr><td>Post-Order Advisory</td><td>Analyse GSTAT order, advise on compliance or appeal to Jharkhand HC at Ranchi under S.113.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
