<section class="steps-section" id="procedure-section">
    <div class="section-container">
        <header class="section-header" style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:48px;">
            <span class="section-eyebrow"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" style="width:18px;height:18px;"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg> Our Process</span>
            <h2 class="section-title">GSTAT Appeal Filing Process at Ranchi Bench - 6 Steps</h2>
            <p>Follow this step-by-step process to file your GSTAT appeal at the Ranchi bench. Patron Accounting's CA team manages every stage.</p>
        </header>
        <div class="steps-container">
            <div class="step-card">
    <div class="step-content"><span class="step-badge">Step 1</span><h3 class="step-title">Assess Appealability</h3><p class="step-description">Verify the demand order from CGST Commissionerate Ranchi, the Dhanbad Sub-Commissionerate, CGST Commissionerate Jamshedpur, or the Commissioner of Commercial Taxes, Jharkhand is appealable under S.112. Patron's CA team reviews the order with particular expertise in mining royalty and steel classification disputes.</p><div class="step-highlights"><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Verify S.112 grounds</span><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Identify commissionerate</span></div></div>
    <div class="step-visual"><div class="step-illustration"><div class="illustration-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="15" y="5" width="90" height="70" rx="6" fill="#F0F4F8" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="30" y1="25" x2="90" y2="25" stroke="#F5A623" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/><line x1="30" y1="40" x2="80" y2="40" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.3"/><line x1="30" y1="52" x2="70" y2="52" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.3"/><circle cx="80" cy="60" r="12" fill="#E8712C" opacity="0.15"/><path d="M76 60l3 3 6-6" stroke="#E8712C" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div><span class="illustration-label">Order Review</span><span class="step-number-large">01</span></div></div>
</div>
<div class="step-card" style="direction:rtl">
    <div class="step-content" style="direction:ltr"><span class="step-badge">Step 2</span><h3 class="step-title">Calculate Pre-deposit</h3><p class="step-description">Compute 20% of disputed tax under S.112(8). Cumulative: 10% from first appeal + 10% for GSTAT. Cap: Rs 20 crore each CGST and SGST. For penalty-only demands under JGST Act, 10% of penalty. Mining and steel sector disputes often involve high-value demands - Patron's team advises on pre-deposit strategy and hardship applications.</p><div class="step-highlights"><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>20% cumulative</span><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Cap Rs 20 crore</span></div></div>
    <div class="step-visual" style="direction:ltr"><div class="step-illustration"><div class="illustration-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="15" y="5" width="90" height="70" rx="6" fill="#F0F4F8" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="30" y1="25" x2="90" y2="25" stroke="#F5A623" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/><line x1="30" y1="40" x2="80" y2="40" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.3"/><line x1="30" y1="52" x2="70" y2="52" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.3"/><circle cx="80" cy="60" r="12" fill="#E8712C" opacity="0.15"/><path d="M76 60l3 3 6-6" stroke="#E8712C" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div><span class="illustration-label">Pre-deposit Paid</span><span class="step-number-large">02</span></div></div>
</div>
<div class="step-card">
    <div class="step-content"><span class="step-badge">Step 3</span><h3 class="step-title">Prepare Form APL-05</h3><p class="step-description">Draft grounds of appeal with consecutively numbered paragraphs. Jharkhand matters frequently involve complex mining royalty GST classification, coal sector ITC, and steel HSN code determinations. Compile supporting documents, obtain certified copies. The GSTAT offline Excel utility generates JSON for upload.</p><div class="step-highlights"><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Mining-specific grounds</span><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Excel utility used</span></div></div>
    <div class="step-visual"><div class="step-illustration"><div class="illustration-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="15" y="5" width="90" height="70" rx="6" fill="#F0F4F8" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="30" y1="25" x2="90" y2="25" stroke="#F5A623" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/><line x1="30" y1="40" x2="80" y2="40" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.3"/><line x1="30" y1="52" x2="70" y2="52" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.3"/><circle cx="80" cy="60" r="12" fill="#E8712C" opacity="0.15"/><path d="M76 60l3 3 6-6" stroke="#E8712C" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div><span class="illustration-label">APL-05 Ready</span><span class="step-number-large">03</span></div></div>
</div>
<div class="step-card" style="direction:rtl">
    <div class="step-content" style="direction:ltr"><span class="step-badge">Step 4</span><h3 class="step-title">File on GSTAT E-Filing Portal</h3><p class="step-description">Submit Form APL-05 at <a href="https://efiling.gstat.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">efiling.gstat.gov.in</a> with pre-deposit proof within 3 months under S.112(1). All Jharkhand filings route to the Ranchi bench - there is no circuit bench. For backlog appeals (orders before 1 April 2026), deadline is 30 June 2026.</p><div class="step-highlights"><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>3-month limitation</span><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>No circuit - all to Ranchi</span></div></div>
    <div class="step-visual" style="direction:ltr"><div class="step-illustration"><div class="illustration-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="15" y="5" width="90" height="70" rx="6" fill="#F0F4F8" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="30" y1="25" x2="90" y2="25" stroke="#F5A623" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/><line x1="30" y1="40" x2="80" y2="40" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.3"/><line x1="30" y1="52" x2="70" y2="52" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.3"/><circle cx="80" cy="60" r="12" fill="#E8712C" opacity="0.15"/><path d="M76 60l3 3 6-6" stroke="#E8712C" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div><span class="illustration-label">E-Filed</span><span class="step-number-large">04</span></div></div>
</div>
<div class="step-card">
    <div class="step-content"><span class="step-badge">Step 5</span><h3 class="step-title">Attend Admission Hearing</h3><p class="step-description">Patron's of-counsel GST litigation specialists with 15+ years of indirect tax experience appear at the Ranchi bench. Hearings in hybrid mode - physical and video conferencing. Businesses in distant districts like Sahibganj, Pakur, and West Singhbhum can attend via video conferencing.</p><div class="step-highlights"><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Hybrid hearing mode</span><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Remote districts covered</span></div></div>
