<!-- SECTION 18: URGENCY CTA -->
<section class="content-section" style="background: var(--orange-lighter) !important; border-left: 4px solid var(--orange);">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <div class="content-text">
                <h2 class="section-title" style="color:var(--orange) !important;">Why You Must Act Now for Your Ranchi GSTAT Appeal</h2><div class="highlight-box" style="background:#FEF2F2;border-left:4px solid #EF4444;padding:20px 24px;border-radius:var(--radius-md);margin-bottom:20px;"><p style="font-weight:700;color:#991B1B;margin-bottom:4px;">Statutory Time Bar - Not Negotiable</p><p>The 3-month limitation under S.112(1) CGST/JGST Act permanently extinguishes the right of appeal. Condonation under S.112(4) is discretionary and the Jharkhand HC has followed the general restrictive approach.</p></div><p>For Jharkhand businesses with orders before 1 April 2026, the backlog deadline is 30 June 2026. Mining and steel sector demands often involve large sums - missing this deadline means permanent loss of the right to challenge multi-crore demands.</p><p>Every day of delay increases pre-deposit complexity as interest compounds. The bench is newly operational. Early filers benefit from shorter admission timelines.</p><p style="font-weight:700;font-size:18px;margin-top:20px;">Contact Patron's team today: <a href="tel:+919459456700">+91 945 945 6700</a> | <a href="https://wa.me/919459456700?text=Hello%2C%20I%20need%20help%20with%20GSTAT%20Appeal%20Filing%20at%20the%20Ranchi%20bench.%20Please%20call%20me." target="_blank" rel="noopener">WhatsApp</a></p>
